@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il27-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il27-tax-years`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance s 41 — "בן זוג שהיה נשוי חלק מהשנה". Row IL-27. Source lines 1689-1692.
--
-- A spouse who is not a registered spouse and was married for part of the tax year is entitled, for computing his tax: (1) for the months
-- in which he was not married, to one twelfth, times those months, of the credit points under ss 34, 36, 40(b) and 40B; (2) for the months
-- in which he was married, to one twelfth, times those months, of the credit points under s 66.
--
-- THE POINTS ARE INPUTS. The whole-year points under ss 34, 36, 40(b) and 40B (rows IL-01, IL-08 and this row) and under s 66 (row IL-02)
-- are the answers of those sections; this section takes them as the caller passes them.
-- A REGISTERED SPOUSE is outside the section ("שאיננו בן זוג רשום"): ss 64B and 65 govern him (row IL-08), which this section does not
-- reach, so it refuses by name.
-- FORK F6: a month in which he was married for part only is, on the face of the text, in neither of "the months in which he was not
-- married" and "the months in which he was married". One named switch (RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08, SHRUG): such a month counts as
-- married; as not married; or as neither; default declined where the readings give different points, answered where they agree.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 41 — a spouse married for part of the tax year`

-- src:1690 | בן זוג שאיננו בן זוג רשום שהיה נשוי בחלק משנת המס יהא זכאי, לענין חישוב המס שהוא חייב בו –
-- src:1691 | (1) בעד תקופה שבה לא היה נשוי – ל־ 1 ⁄ 12 מנקודות הזיכוי לפי סעיפים 34, 36, 40(ב) ו־40ב כפול במספר החדשים בשנת המס שבהם לא היה נשוי;
-- src:1692 | (2) בעד התקופה שבה היה נשוי – ל־ 1 ⁄ 12 מנקודות הזיכוי לפי סעיף 66 כפול במספר החדשים בשנת המס שבהם היה נשוי.

@ref ITO s 41, line 1690 ("שאיננו בן זוג רשום")
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 41 does not apply to a registered spouse, whose tax is under sections 64B and 65` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 41 does not apply to a registered spouse, whose tax is under sections 64B and 65"

@ref ITO s 41, lines 1691-1692
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the months of the tax year given for section 41 do not add up to twelve` MEANS
    REFUSE "the months of the tax year given for section 41 do not add up to twelve"

@ref ITO s 41, lines 1691-1692; fork F6
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 41 does not say in which list a month of part marriage is, and here the readings differ` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 41 does not say in which list a month of part marriage is, and here the readings differ"

@ref ITO s 41, lines 1691-1692; fork F6; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of a month in which he was married for part, for section 41`
`section 41 — the reading row IL-27 takes of a month in which he was married for part` MEANS
    `declined where the readings differ`

-- (1) and (2): one twelfth of the points, times the months, for each side.
@ref ITO s 41(1), (2), lines 1691-1692
GIVEN nm IS A NUMBER
      wm IS A NUMBER
      i  IS A `A spouse married for part of the tax year, for section 41`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 41 — the points for` nm `months not married and` wm `months married, for` i MEANS
    (nm TIMES i's `credit points for the whole year under sections 34, 36, 40(b) and 40B, as if not married`
     PLUS wm TIMES i's `credit points for the whole year under section 66, as if married`) DIVIDED BY 12

@ref ITO s 41, lines 1690-1692; fork F6
GIVEN r IS A `A reading of a month in which he was married for part, for section 41`
      i IS A `A spouse married for part of the tax year, for section 41`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 41, reading a month married for part as` r `, for` i MEANS
    `for tax year` (i's `tax year`) `, row IL-27 answers`
        (BRANCH
            IF   i's `a registered spouse`
            THEN `section 41 does not apply to a registered spouse, whose tax is under sections 64B and 65`
            IF   NOT (i's `months of the tax year in which he was not married` PLUS i's `months of the tax year in which he was married` PLUS i's `months of the tax year in which he was married for part of the month` EQUALS 12)
            THEN `the months of the tax year given for section 41 do not add up to twelve`
            OTHERWISE
                CONSIDER r
                WHEN `a month in which he was married` THEN `as married`
                WHEN `a month in which he was not married` THEN `as not married`
                WHEN `a month of neither` THEN `as neither`
                WHEN `declined where the readings differ`
                    THEN IF   `as married` EQUALS `as not married` AND `as not married` EQUALS `as neither`
                         THEN `as married`
                         ELSE `section 41 does not say in which list a month of part marriage is, and here the readings differ`)
    WHERE
        `not`   MEANS i's `months of the tax year in which he was not married`
        `wed`   MEANS i's `months of the tax year in which he was married`
        `part`  MEANS i's `months of the tax year in which he was married for part of the month`
        `as married`     MEANS `s 41 — the points for` `not` `months not married and` (`wed` PLUS `part`) `months married, for` i
        `as not married` MEANS `s 41 — the points for` (`not` PLUS `part`) `months not married and` `wed` `months married, for` i
        `as neither`     MEANS `s 41 — the points for` `not` `months not married and` `wed` `months married, for` i

@export The credit points under Income Tax Ordinance s 41 (a spouse, not a registered spouse, married for part of the tax year) for a tax year from 2024: one twelfth of the whole-year points under ss 34, 36, 40(b) and 40B for each month not married and one twelfth of the points under s 66 for each month married; declines for a registered spouse, where the months do not add up, and where a month of part marriage changes the answer
@ref ITO s 41, lines 1689-1692
GIVEN i IS A `A spouse married for part of the tax year, for section 41`
          @desc the tax year, whether he is a registered spouse, the months of the year not married, married, and married for part of the month, and the whole-year points under ss 34, 36, 40(b) and 40B and under s 66, which other sections answer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 41 for` i MEANS
    `the credit points under section 41, reading a month married for part as` `section 41 — the reading row IL-27 takes of a month in which he was married for part` `, for` i
